                <pb facs="0720" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1934v05/pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">810.5151 Williams Mission/24: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gibson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-07-17T19:00:00-04:00">July 17, 1934—7 p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>83. For Doctor Williams. Recent developments in the exchange situation in Uruguay
                    prejudicial to American interests make it seem highly important that you visit
                    Montevideo and study the problem there. I very much hope that you will find it
                    possible to do so, even though this may mean extending your trip 10 days or 2
                    weeks longer.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
